        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Draft: add CLI catalog views",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nDraft review PR for the CLI catalog effort described in the RFC:\n\n- RFC PR: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/32\n- RFC branch/file: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/rfcs/blob/codex/cli-catalog-overlay-rfc/rfcs/0010-cli-catalog-overlay.md\n\nThis adds a read-only catalog view over existing OpenClaw command/tool surfaces rather than a second command system. It covers:\n\n- `openclaw catalog list` JSON/Markdown output\n- runtime command, plugin descriptor, and supplied node/operator command lenses\n- prompt projection from catalog metadata, including a scoped `node-operator` prompt view\n- audit, test-matrix, and operator summary views\n- schema fixtures, generated docs, and advisory report artifacts\n- plugin descriptor catalog metadata preservation through registry normalization\n\nThe goal is to make commands, routed operations, plugin commands, node/operator commands, prompt-visible surfaces, audit views, and operator/test planning easier to inspect and discuss from one place.\n\n## Scout / node-mode evidence\n\nNode/operator support is now folded through the six-PR stack instead of being staged as a separate follow-up. The live motivation is the node-mode work in `gim-home/m`:\n\n- `gim-home/m#4045`: node-routed MCP commands such as `mcp.help`, `mcp.invoke`, `mcp.status`, and `mcp.cancel`\n- `gim-home/m#4086`: filesystem node commands such as `filesystem.read`, `filesystem.write`, and `filesystem.patch`\n- `gim-home/m#4088`: browser/file-open node commands such as `browser.open` and `file.openWithDefaultApp`\n\nThat stack shows why the catalog needs scoped lenses, not just broad inventory. A node-operating agent needs a small prompt view of available node commands, argument hints, risk, confirmation, and approval boundaries that match the actual Desktop/Gateway implementation.\n\n## Proposed stack\n\nThis draft PR contains the six catalog slices folded together for directional review:\n\n1. Foundation catalog view, including the supplied `cli.nodeCommands` contract\n2. Dynamic inventory and operator lenses, including node command audit/test/summary fields\n3. Prompt projection, including the scoped `node-operator` prompt view\n4. Schema fixtures for list/audit/test-matrix/summary/prompt contracts\n5. Generated reference docs\n6. Hardening, advisory reports, plugin metadata preservation, and consumer boundary\n\nThe same stack is also prepared as fork-local draft PRs so reviewers can inspect it one layer at a time:\n\n- PR1 foundation: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/11\n- PR2 dynamic/operator lenses: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/12\n- PR3 prompt projection: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/13\n- PR4 schema fixtures: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/14\n- PR5 generated docs: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/15\n- PR6 hardening and consumer contract: https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/16\n\nThose fork-local PRs are review aids, not a request to merge from the fork. If maintainers prefer separate upstream implementation PRs, I am happy to open the same stack against `openclaw/openclaw` and merge it in order.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/cli-catalog-overlay-list.test.ts test/scripts/generate-cli-catalog-doc.test.ts src/cli-catalog-overlay/schema-fixtures.test.ts src/cli-catalog-overlay/prompt-projection.test.ts src/cli-catalog-overlay/list.test.ts src/cli-catalog-overlay/operator-summary.test.ts src/cli/catalog-cli.test.ts --reporter=dot`\n- `npm exec -- oxfmt --check <review-touched files>`\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- One `codex review` per branch diff passed after fixes: PR1 vs `origin/main`, then PR2-PR6 against the previous stack branch.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis is opened as a draft so maintainers can comment on direction, API shape, docs, and whether this should remain one review PR or be split into the smaller stacked branches above.",
        "branch": "user/giodl/cli-catalog-review-hardening",
